{
  "version": 1,
  "_about": [
    "One rule set for which servers and libraries Nostalgex lists, starts on and reads (N-016 option A, Chad's go 2026-11-15). The contract is the web tuner and Docker's scripts/nostalgex-library-picker.js (rules 1 to 7 in its header) and its storage in scripts/nostalgex-library-selection.js, read by scripts/nostalgex-library-picker-smoke.mjs (npm run test:library-picker). The Apple TV (LibrarySectionRef, LibrarySectionSelectionStore, AppState+Auth), the Roku (PlexLibrary.brs NxPlexSectionRefs, SettingsRail.brs, HiddenLibraries.brs, MediaBrowserLibrary.brs) and Android (PlexLibrary.kt, MediaBrowserLibrary.kt, LibrarySection.kt) are to match it.",
    "Plain JSON, no code in it, so Swift (Codable), BrightScript (ParseJson) and Kotlin (kotlinx.serialization or org.json) read it the way they read jellyfin-library-golden.json. Ids in expected values are `<serverId>::<sectionKey>` (rule 6); the server id is each platform's own stable string for a server (web: a Plex server's machineIdentifier, or its name when it has none; a Jellyfin or Emby server's address), so it is only ever compared whole.",
    "A library is on or off. Two saved lists make that: `off` (ids the viewer switched OFF; every library but a hidden one reads it) and `includedHidden` (ids of hidden Jellyfin libraries the viewer switched ON; a hidden library reads only this). Everything starts ON except a hidden Jellyfin library. These are the Apple TV's two sets (nostalgex_deselected_library_sections and nostalgex_included_hidden_library_sections).",
    "`plexListing`: servers answer /library/sections; `sections` null is a server that did not answer. `listed` is what the picker and Settings show, in order. Only type movie and show are listed and read (a Music or Photo library never is). `label` is the kind shown (Movies, TV Shows, Music Videos); `musicVideo` is the name rule (music video, music, mv, mvs, case ignored) that marks a Plex library's items as music videos for HIGH ROTATION, unchanged. `subtitle` is the line under the name: the kind, with the server name first when the listing spans more than one server, then HIDDEN ON JELLYFIN for a hidden library.",
    "`mediaBrowserListing`: Jellyfin or Emby views. `shown` is the plain /UserViews (Emby: /Users/{id}/Views) answer, `all` the answer with includeHidden=true (null: not asked, which is every Emby, or the ask failed). A view only in `all` is hidden; a view in `shown` and not in `all` is kept (the union, in the order of `all` then the rest of `shown`); a view whose CollectionType holds no videos is never listed, hidden or not. Hidden libraries start off.",
    "`serverDefaults`: which Plex servers start on at first setup: the viewer's own (`owned`), or all of them when none is owned, in list order.",
    "`reads`: given the listed libraries (`hidden` as listed) and the two saved lists, the ids a scan reads, in listed order. Ids saved for a server that did not answer, or for a library the server no longer lists, change nothing.",
    "`choices`: the saved lists after the viewer switches the named libraries, one after another (a library on goes off, off goes on). Only the touched id moves; every other saved id stays, including ids for a server that did not answer. Lists compare as sets.",
    "`hiddenSwitchUpgrade`: Android and the web tuner (until now) had ONE switch for all hidden Jellyfin libraries, off by default. On upgrade, with the switch on and the hidden libraries known (`hiddenKnown`: the includeHidden list was answered), each hidden library not in `off` goes into `includedHidden` once and the old switch is cleared (`done`). With the hidden libraries not yet known, nothing changes and the old switch is kept (`done` false). Switch off or never set: nothing to carry, `done` true."
  ],
